{"hits": {"hits": [{"created": "1985-05-01T00:00:00+00:00", "updated": "2023-03-07T03:03:05.807590+00:00", "id": "16613", "metadata": {"publication_info": [{"journal_volume": "263", "page_end": "648", "year": 1986, "page_start": "637", "journal_title": "Nucl.Phys.B"}, {"pubinfo_freetext": "Also in *Le Guillou, J.C. (ed.), Zinn-Justin, J. (ed.): Large-order behaviour of perturbation theory* 508-519"}], "authors": [{"full_name": "David, F."}], "texkeys": ["David:1985xj"], "imprints": [{"date": "1986"}], "abstracts": [{"value": "Recently, the ITEP group has analysed the structure of the operator product expansion in the 1/ N expansion of some two-dimensional models. We show that, despite their claim, their analysis does not invalidate the conclusions of previous studies by the present author on the role of renormalon singularities in the operation product expansion. Some considerations on the applicability of the operator product expansion in QCD are also developed."}], "control_number": 16613, "dois": [{"value": "10.1016/0550-3213(86)90279-8"}], "titles": [{"title": "The Operator Product Expansion and Renormalons: A Comment"}, {"title": "THE OPERATOR PRODUCT EXPANSION AND RENORMALONS: A COMMENT"}], "author_count": 1, "document_type": ["article"]}, "links": {"bibtex": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/16613?format=bibtex", "latex-eu": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/16613?format=latex-eu", "latex-us": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/16613?format=latex-us", "json": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/16613?format=json", "json-expanded": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/16613?format=json-expanded", "cv": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/16613?format=cv", "citations": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=refersto%3Arecid%3A16613"}}], "total": 1}, "links": {"self": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?sort=mostcited&q=j%20Nucl.Phys.B%2C263%2C637&size=3&page=1&fields=control_number,titles.title,authors.full_name,author_count,publica